{
  "dom_id": "step-q145909",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x,y),$ where\n\n$$\nF(7,1)=\\frac{9}{16},\\,F(7,-2)=\\frac{1}{4},\\,F(3,1)=\\frac{1}{8},\\,F(3,-2)=\\frac{1}{16},\n$$\n\nand the supports of $X$ and $Y$, respectively, are\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\},\\,{S}_{Y}=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.\n$$\n\nFind $P(5\\le X\\le 8,-1\\le Y\\le 1).$",
